   "source": [
    "### Data Augmentation\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "We decided to **Budget-Aware augmentation**. In this method where we only create new augmentated images if the classes inside that image still need more samples. Every class has a \"budget\": a target number of samples it should reach. The reason behind this choice is there are many crops containing multiple classes. Lets say one crop has one of the popular classes and one of the rare classes. If we augment this crop it will increase both classes which we are trying to avoid.\n",
    "\n",
    "In this method:\n",
    "\n",
    "- We count our classes\n",
    "- Set a target for each class\n",
    "- Look at each cropped image\n",
    "- Try an augmentation\n",
    "- Check the budget\n",
    "- Update counts\n",
    "\n",
    "This method has some pros:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Fixes class imbalance** correctly\n",
    "- **Avoids over-sampling** popular classes\n",
    "- **Uses real data** naturally\n",
    "- **Works well with cluster based** crops\n",
    "- **Prevents overfitting** for small classes\n",
    "- Automatically **adjusts to multiclass crops**\n",
    "\n",
    "However, it also has some cons:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Some crops **cannot be used** (1 rare class, 3 popular class)\n",
    "- **Slow** if many classes\n",
    "- May require **splitting**\n",
    "- We **won't reach perfect balance**\n",
    "- Implementation is **more complex**\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Implementation\n",
    "\n",
    "Key steps:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Count classes\n",
    "    - Read all label ```.txt``` files.\n",
    "    - Count how many times each class id appears. This is ```current_count```\n",
    "- Choose target per class\n",
    "    - Decide target samples for each class. (e.g. 40% of the largest class, or fixed number like 600.\n",
    "    - For each class calculate ```target = max(current_count, chosen_target)``` so we never lower counts\n",
    "- Calculate deficits\n",
    "    - For every class: ```deficit = target - current_count```\n",
    "    - Keep only classes with ```deficit > 0```.\n",
    "- List candidate crops\n",
    "    - Make a list of our cropped images (each crop has image and label)\n",
    "    - Keep only crops that contain at least one class with deficit. These are candidates.\n",
    "- Score candidates\n",
    "    - Give each candidate a simple score: ```(rare_count) / (1 + popular_count)```.\n",
    "    - Rare_count = number of deficit classes in crop. Popular_count = other classes in crop.\n",
    "    - Sort candidates from best score to worst (more rare, less popular first).\n",
    "- Try augmentation for each candidate\n",
    "    - Load crop image and its labels.\n",
    "    - Apply augmentation (photometric + small geometric) using bbox-aware library.\n",
    "    - If augmentation removes all boxes, discard this trial.\n",
    "- Budget check before saving\n",
    "    - Find classes present in the augmented crop and how many boxes for each.\n",
    "    - For each class in augmented crop check: if ```current_count + add > target``` then reject this augmented sample.\n",
    "    - If none exceed target then accept and save the augmented image and label.\n",
    "- Update running counts\n",
    "    - When we save an augmented sample, increase ```current_count``` for every class found in it.\n",
    "    - Recompute ```deficit = max(0, target - current_count)``` for those classes.\n",
    "- If candidate violates budget, try split\n",
    "    - For a mixed crop (rare + popular), try to make a smaller crop centered on the rare bbox (add small margin).\n",
    "    - Augment the split crop and do the same budget check. If OK then save it. If not then skip.\n",
    "- Repeat passes until done\n",
    "    - Loop over candidates in passes. Stop when:\n",
    "        - All deficits are filled, or\n",
    "        - No progress in a pass (no new saved augmentations).\n",
    "- Record manifest\n",
    "    - Save a CSV that lists each saved augmentation: source crop, new file path, classes inside. This helps auditing.\n",
    "- Validation and final checks\n",
    "    - Visual check: inspect many saved augmented images to ensure boxes align.\n",
    "    - Re-count classes to confirm targets reached.\n",
    "    - Keep validation/test sets unchanged (no augmented variants inside val/test).\n",
    "- If deficits remain\n",
    "    - Use copy-paste instance augmentation: extract rare objects and paste onto neutral backgrounds (respect budget).\n",
    "    - Or increase target fraction slightly if practical.\n",
    "- Training note\n",
    "    - Train with mixture: augmented crops + some original full images. This keeps context and prevents overfitting."
   ]
  },
